{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":820,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.83","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 83","reference":"Psalms 83","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"A remonstrance of the designs and endeavours of Israel's enemies, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-8.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"A prayer, that God would defeat them, preserve his church, and get himself glory, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"9-18.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"A song or psalm of Asaph.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":7,"text":"Hidden ones - Thy people of Israel, who are called God's hidden or secret ones, to intimate the respect which God has to them, as to his peculiar treasure.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":8,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":9,"text":"The tabernacles - The people dwelling in them.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":10,"text":"Ishmaelites - Some of the posterity of Ishmael, called by their father's name, as others of them are supposed to be called Hagarens from their grandmother Hagar.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":11,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":12,"text":"Gebal - An Arabian people so called by ancient writers dwelling in the southern border of Canaan, where most of the people here mentioned had their abode.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":13,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":14,"text":"Of Lot - Moab and Ammon.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":15,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":16,"text":"A wheel - Whereas they promise to themselves a sure possession, let them be like a wheel, which is very unstable, and soon removed.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":17,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":18,"text":"The mountains - The woods upon the mountains, which in those hot countries, when they have once taken fire, burn with irresistible violence.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":19,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":20,"text":"May seek - May own and worship thee as the only true God.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":83}}